                <pb facs="0954" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg834"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/254: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva
                        (Gilbert)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-12T17:00:00-05:00">October 12, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Department is announcing appointment of Mr. Edmond E. Day, Director of
                    Social Science, Rockefeller Foundation, and Professor John H. Williams, Harvard
                    University, as American representatives on preparatory committee of experts for
                    the Monetary and Economic Conference. They will sail on Steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Exeter</hi> October 18th and should reach Geneva October
                    29.</p>
                <p>Please inform Secretary General.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
